Based on github.com/coder/websocket v1.8.15, retaining its MIT license.

Campfire adds prepared.go, batch.go and their tests. PreparedMessage shares immutable
payloads and lazily compressed bytes across server connections negotiating
permessage-deflate without context takeover. WritePreparedBatch writes many prepared
messages to such a connection as one vectored write (writev on TCP) under one write
deadline, the way the reference's cable socket writes (reference/crates/cable/src/socket.rs).
Other connection modes use Write. The existing frame writer still handles locking,
cancellation and close state; batches take the same locks.
No upstream Go source files were changed. Upstream tests run in bin/check.
